      "body": "## Summary\n\nTell the model when its conversation memory was cut, replaced, unavailable, or replayed with reduced fidelity. A gateway-authored system notice precedes history on the current request, and one `gateway.memory.notice` event carries the same fact kinds. Nothing from the notice enters recorded history.\n\nThe notice type lives with `SessionInputs` in dekopon-agent. r28 B4's counted omission line is meant to reuse this definition; this PR implements no part of B4.\n\n## Security impact\n\nModel-facing text only. No authority, credential, grant, network destination or provider changes. The notice is gateway-authored prompt text and grants nothing (\"Memory never becomes authority\").\n\n## Validation\n\nFix pass 1 for coordinator Astra R158: F1 and F2 addressed at `9c35c572dd942750213b29dcb5e084e70401a901`, on top of reviewed head `18e816165880403a697520f1fc438182801cac5d`. F3 is inherited and out of scope; summarization/admission behavior is unchanged.\n\n| Head | Toolchain | Gate | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 9c35c572 | Git / Rust 1.98.1 | `git diff --check`; `cargo fmt --all --check` | Pass |\n| 9c35c572 | Rust 1.98.1 | `RUST_LOG=info DEKOPON_TEST_BROKERD=\"$PWD/target/debug/dekopon-brokerd\" cargo test -p dekopon-agent -p dekopon-gatewayd --all-features --locked --lib --bins --tests` | Pass: 1,284 tests, including 189 agent and 1,044 gatewayd library tests and 16 real-daemon integration tests |\n| 9c35c572 | Rust 1.98.1 | `cargo test -p dekopon-gatewayd --all-features --locked --lib tests::memory_notice` | Pass: 12 SessionRunner regressions |\n| 9c35c572 | Rust 1.98.1 | `cargo clippy -p dekopon-agent -p dekopon-gatewayd --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings` | Pass |\n| 9c35c572 | Rust 1.98.1 | `RUSTDOCFLAGS=\"-D warnings\" cargo doc -p dekopon-agent -p dekopon-gatewayd --all-features --no-deps --locked` | Pass |\n| 9c35c572 | Rust 1.98.1 | `cargo test -p dekopon-agent -p dekopon-gatewayd --all-features --locked --doc` | Pass: no doctests in these crates |\n| 9c35c572 | cargo-deny | `cargo deny --all-features check` | Pass: advisories, bans, licenses and sources |\n| 9c35c572 | Python 3 / Bash | Documentation duplicate gate and CI's audit-event documentation gate | Pass: 49 documents / 45 audit event names |\n| prior setup | Rust / shell | Broker binary and checksum-verified external fixtures | Retained from initial pass; reused by the passing real-daemon tests |\n| 9c35c572 | CI | Workspace tests, aggregate quality, OpenObserve, CLI smoke, packaging/container verification and both ARM64 checks | Pass: [CI run 40403568409](https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon/actions/runs/40403568409); local OpenObserve remains blocked by the previously observed image-download Forbidden |\n| 9c35c572 | CI | F3: `memory-lab scenarios` / `summarizer-hang (required)` | [Attempt 1](https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon/actions/runs/40403568363/attempts/1) failed only summarizer-hang and the enforcing summary; [attempt 2](https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon/actions/runs/40403568363/attempts/2) rerun requested, pending |\n\nF1's `additive_summary_parts_count_their_source_once_in_the_notice` drives SessionRunner with a 1,000-byte source, 100- and 200-byte current-version additive parts, and a stale-version part. The actual model request must show 700 omitted bytes and the combined 300-byte body. It fails if only one part is subtracted, the source is added per part, or stale-version text is counted.\n\nF2's `a_bash_turn_followed_by_resident_replay_reports_that_bash_is_not_kept` observes a real bash result in the first session and checks the following request's conversation-only notice and absent bash result. The old unconditional bash-retention claim fails that assertion. Additional SessionRunner cases check platform recall and mixed journal/resident replay. Existing journal-only request assertions retain their journal fidelity expectation.\n\nThe complete suites use the application's normal `RUST_LOG=info`; the workspace's inherited error-only filter suppresses a recovery test's expected warning. Build artifacts are retained for the coordinator's next review and can be removed when that gate resolves.\n\n## Limitations / follow-ups\n\nThe PR remains draft while the inherited memory-lab failure is unresolved. The pinned [steering](https://github.com/xrl/agents/blob/cc070358504191cc739c6aaecf124e91da8682aa/steering/GPT.md) says, \"Open it ready for review only if every gate passed,\" and requires reporting/rerunning unrelated CI failures without pushing a fix for them. [Current run 40390609000, attempt 1](https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon/actions/runs/40390609000/attempts/1) failed only `summarizer-hang (required)` and the enforcing summary. [Pre-existing run 40361947330](https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon/actions/runs/40361947330) failed those same steps at `2f0c50d93cd5cb6e5abbbe348c437c1c96169c8b`, whose tree is identical to the requested base: both have tree `87d66279195cccb1a973cd75b30918742663eda0`. The unchanged gate is `.github/workflows/memory-lab.yml:135`, pinned to harness `63eee72f78797a2ea637a4cfdb69202487e13099`. The failed job was rerun as steering requires ([attempt 2](https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon/actions/runs/40390609000/attempts/2)); it reproduced the same two failed steps on predecessor `c4fab67a`. The same inherited check failed on reviewed head `18e81616` in [run 40395359382](https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon/actions/runs/40395359382). On fix head `9c35c572`, [run 40403568363, attempt 1](https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon/actions/runs/40403568363/attempts/1) reproduced only the inherited summarizer-hang failure and enforcing summary. All other CI checks passed. The failed job was rerun as steering requires; [attempt 2](https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon/actions/runs/40403568363/attempts/2) is pending. This F3 gate alone forces draft status; it is explicitly out of scope for this fix pass. This environment's network policy returns Forbidden for the run logs and evidence artifact, so the detailed failed assertion is unavailable here.\n\nCoordinator-launched Astra R158 blocked on F1/F2; those fixes await the coordinator\u2019s fresh review over the immutable SHAs. This executor does not self-certify that review. Base: `6b47a4aa0ab3d3711758df35cb2f8ae5de73fff2`.\n\nCoordinator post-deploy `cm watch`: within 72 hours of the sync, observe `log:gateway.memory.notice` with `memory.notice.kinds` containing `window-omission` in a DekoponVille DM thread past 12 turns, and confirm that the model's reply in that turn no longer claims to see the first message. This PR performs no live check or deployment.\n\n## Choices I made\n\n- Carry projection history, typed facts and the first shown record in an internal `Projected` result; leave journal `Line`, envelopes and all frozen contracts unchanged.\n- Peek at most one extra line in the existing projection scan to distinguish an eligible older tail from EOF or a grant boundary; add no file, broker call, model call or concurrency primitive.\n- Count only individually known omissions inside the scanned window in `memory.records.omitted`; report the uncounted older tail through `window-omission`, without inferring counts from record IDs.\n- Keep record IDs and omitted byte counts in named u64 fields, matching existing journal and Representation types; MemoryNotice privately enforces the rendered-byte ceiling.\n- Preserve horizon/seal eligibility: WindowOmission reports eligible older records only, as required by that fact.\n- Use the existing system-message encoding for the request-only notice, after instructions and skills and before history; user text cannot occupy that role.\n- Collapse ID lists longer than two entries to counts, with total omitted bytes for replacement groups; keep all applicable fact kinds within a private 1024-byte ceiling and warn/skip if rendering cannot fit.\n- Preserve the existing `task` recall-failure reason alongside `JournalError::label()`'s `io` and `corrupt`, and carry cold recall failure facts through a reset that leaves projection an absent file.\n- Require both the seeded recall and final projection to be empty for a thread-without-memory fact; decide replies from thread/message IDs, never transport names.\n- Follow the brief's one-sentence documentation scope where inference.md's existing drop list is broader than journal replay; the added sentence explicitly identifies retained bash exchanges.\n- Update existing request positions and expected system messages instead of filtering notices out of the fake model's captured requests.\n- Exceed the approximately 300-line target: the complete PR adds 907 lines and removes 55, including twelve real SessionRunner regressions, typed telemetry capture, bounded-rendering coverage and affected existing request assertions.\n- Follow the brief's 300-word final-report cap over the steering file's full-diff report requirement; the reviewable diff remains in this PR.\n- Preserve the notice scope while rerunning the inherited memory-lab failure; pinned steering explicitly requires reporting both runs and pushing no fix for unrelated CI failures.\n- State recall/projection failure without claiming an in-memory-only fallback, because projection can recover after cold recall fails.\n\n- F1: subtract all current-version selected parts from the largest shared captured source size once; use the same helper for envelope metadata and notice facts, preserving envelope format.\n- F2: derive Journal, Conversation or Mixed provenance from the turns surviving fitting; default platform, seeded recall and projection-error fallback to Conversation.\n- Qualify mixed replay explicitly rather than claiming bash retention for resident turns; update the existing inference sentence and request expectations accordingly.\n- Follow this fix brief's explicit PR-body update instruction over the pinned fix-round instruction to leave the body alone; keep fix commits free of Changelog lines.\n\n",
